# CAPTURED, NOT INVENTED — see docs/dev/TESTING.md § "Fixtures captured from
# reality". Real `usage` and `compact_boundary` objects lifted verbatim from the
# maintainer's own transcripts on 2026-08-07, then scrubbed: free text replaced
# with synthetic strings, every uuid replaced with the deterministic scenario
# form, and `cwd`/`gitBranch`/`timestamp`/`version`/`requestId` dropped outright
# rather than truncated. The numbers and the KEY ORDER are untouched, because
# the key order is the whole point — a substring parser that happened to work on
# an invented line is exactly the failure this file exists to prevent.
#
# Field measurement, 2026-08-07: 731 of 750 transcripts carry `"usage":{`.
# Only 1 of 750 carries `"subtype":"compact_boundary"` — compaction is rare in
# this corpus because the maintainer clears far more often than he compacts, so
# the anchoring path rests on a single field sample. Re-measure with:
#   find ~/.claude/projects -name '*.jsonl' | wc -l
#   grep -rl '"usage":{' --include='*.jsonl' ~/.claude/projects | wc -l
#   grep -rl '"subtype":"compact_boundary"' --include='*.jsonl' ~/.claude/projects | wc -l
#
# Note the decoys, all of them real and all of them load-bearing for the parser:
#   - `cache_creation` nests `ephemeral_*_input_tokens`
#   - `iterations` repeats every usage key, once per inference step
#   - `output_tokens` sits between the counts that ARE summed
#   - `preTokens` precedes `postTokens` on the boundary line
# Lines 1-3 are the pre-compaction conversation; the boundary and the line after
# it are what a session looks like immediately post-`/compact`.
